    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1536-26": {
      "title": "Technician",
      "description": "1536-26 Technician - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Technician School Operations (COO) Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £27,319 to £29,588\r\n            per annum, depending on experience Grade: Grade 06 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (12 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Friday 06 November 2026 Interview Date: Monday 07 December 2026 Reference: 1536-26 Release Date: Friday 09 October 2026 Job Title: Laboratory Technician Aston University is a leading university in the heart of Birmingham, known for its focus on employability, real‑world impact and an inclusive, supportive culture. The School of Medicine, Pharmacy and Biosciences delivers high-quality, practice-focused teaching in well-equipped laboratories, providing an excellent environment for staff and students to develop their skills and careers. The opportunity An exciting opportunity has arisen to join our amazing technical team within School Operations on a 12-month fixed term contract to provide maternity cover. We are seeking a proactive, reliable individual to join our team which supports teaching and research facilities in the School of Medicine, Pharmacy and Biosciences. The successful candidate will join the Laboratory Operations team, where you will provide day to day technical support for our teaching facilities across Biosciences, Pharmaceutics, and Neuroscience subject groups. This is a varied and rewarding role where you will work closely with technical colleagues, academic staff, and students to ensure our laboratories run smoothly, safely, and effectively. The main responsibilities of this role include: Liaising with academic stakeholders and technical colleagues to understand and support teaching programmes. Preparing laboratories, materials, and equipment for practical class sessions including purchasing chemicals and consumables. Demonstrating and instructing students in practical techniques. Assisting with inventories, purchasing, stock control, consumable issues, storekeeping, deliveries and laboratory waste management. Promoting safe working practices, providing health and safety advice, and ensuring laboratory facilities are compliant. Contributing positively to a supportive, inclusive and collaborative team environment, working effectively with colleagues, and supporting the sharing of knowledge, skills, and best practices. About you We are looking for a practical, organised, proactive individual with a strong commitment to teamwork and customer service. You will thrive in a busy, dynamic environment and enjoy working collaboratively with a diverse range of people, from students to academic staff and external suppliers. Excellent communication skills and a strong attention to detail are essential for supporting practical classes and demonstrating equipment. The successful candidate will hold a degree or equivalent qualifications in a subject relevant to the role, experience of working in a laboratory setting in Pharmaceutics or Biosciences is essential although full training will be provided. Working at Aston We are committed to the Technician Commitment and to supporting the career development of technical staff across all disciplines. You will be supported to undertake a range of training and development activity, as a minimum, you will undertake relevant technical and health & safety training. Aston University is located within Birmingham city centre and benefits from excellent transport links by bus and train. Discounted on-site parking and a cycle-to-work scheme are also available. Information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . For further Information, please contact the Technical Team Leader - Lindsay Hathaway l.hathaway@aston.ac.uk Please visit our website http://www.aston.ac.uk/jobs for further information and to apply online. Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Senior Leisure Assistant ( Internal Only ) Research Associate in Mathematics Postdoctoral Research Associate - Membrane Protein Folding View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1640-26": {
      "title": "1640-26 Compliance Officer",
      "description": "1640-26 Compliance Officer - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Compliance Officer Estates & Capital Developments Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £38,784 to £46,049\n            per annum (pro-rata) Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Fixed Term\n              \n                (12 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Sunday 08 November 2026 Interview Date: Thursday 19 November 2026 Reference: 1640-26 Release Date: Thursday 15 October 2026 This is a full-time 12 month fixed term contract to cover maternity leave, The role will cover Fire, Legionella, building safety, governance, and maintenance. You will also be establishing and leading a compliance team. You will be managing the delivery of all compliance inspections delivered both in-house and by external contractors. You will review all compliance records and raise defects and jobs for both engineering and maintenance teams. You will be maintaining accurate asset registers of equipment, statutory inspections and maintenance contracts. What you'll need to succeed You will have a track record of delivering compliance at a high level and of establishing and leading a team. You will be confident collaborating with senior stakeholders and in reporting into senior team members. You will ideally have a degree in a relevant subject, Legionella RP training, LOLER and PSSR training. You will also have outstanding knowledge of Fire Safety standards in a higher education context. What you'll get in return You will benefit from working in a socially motivated and passionate team, with an outstanding culture of support and development. You will enjoy 30 days holiday plus bank holidays, generous pension contributions, staff wellbeing benefits and discounted meals on site. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 25 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor those who are already on a Skilled Worker Visa issued before 04 April 2024 or 22 July 2025. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting.See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate Compliance Officer Administration & Research Officer (Internal only) View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
