    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1750-26": {
      "title": "Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term)",
      "description": "1750-26 Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) Aston Business School Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £48,337 to £57,666 Grade: Grade 09 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (12 months) Basis: Part Time\r\n            (0.4) Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Thursday 12 November 2026 Interview Date: Friday 27 November 2026 Reference: 1750-26 Release Date: Friday 23 October 2026 Aston Business School is triple accredited (EQUIS, AACSB and AMBA). The Leadership and Management Department at Aston Business School is a vibrant, interdisciplinary community dedicated to advancing responsible leadership, ethical business practices, and healthy, inclusive workplaces. About the Role We are seeking to appoint a Lecturer (Teaching only) in People Management to contribute to the teaching profile of the Department. We particularly welcome applications from candidates with interests or experience related to organisational behaviour, wellbeing, talent management, HRM . This role is ideally suited to a teaching-focused academic or practitioner-academic who is passionate about high-quality, inclusive education and practice-informed learning. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching across foundation, undergraduate, postgraduate, and apprenticeship programmes , and play an active role in curriculum development and student support. Appointment may be made at Grade 8 or Grade 9 , depending on experience. Key Responsibilities Teaching and Learning Deliver high-quality teaching and assessment across foundation, undergraduate, and postgraduate programmes. Contribute to the design, development, and review of modules and curricula, with increasing independence at Grade 9. Provide academic advice, guidance, and pastoral support to students. Employ innovative, inclusive, and digitally enabled teaching and assessment approaches. Engage in quality assurance processes, including module evaluation and feedback analysis. Why Join Aston? We offer a stimulating research environment, support for international conference participation, research mentoring, and a commitment to career development. Our department is deeply engaged in real-world impact, working closely with healthcare organisations, professional bodies, and public sector partners. The post-holders will report to the Head of Department. For informal discussions relating to this post please contact the Deputy Head of Department, Dr. Matthew Carter.   E-mail ( m.r.carter@aston.ac.uk ). Further Information Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community. We promote equality and diversity in all aspects of our work and support an inclusive environment where colleagues can confidently be themselves. Learn more: Inclusive Aston For alternative formats or accessibility needs, please contact: recruitment@aston.ac.uk To apply, visit: http://www.aston.ac.uk/jobs This role does not meet the eligibility criteria for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. See here for information about Skilled Worker eligibility criteria: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) Apprentice Technician Lecturer in Biochemistry View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
